# 3. `opportunities`

Keep the shared core relatively small.

```sql
opportunities
-------------
id uuid

source_id
market_id
external_id

kind
title
description

status

reward_model
reward_asset
reward_usd

created_at
deadline_at
closed_at

competition_count

human_level
capital_required_usd

raw_latest jsonb

first_seen_at
last_seen_at
```

Don't add 200 nullable columns for Bittensor-specific weirdness.

Put that in:

```text
raw_latest JSONB
```

and promote fields into typed columns only when they become broadly useful.

Postgres `jsonb` is indexed/queryable, so this hybrid approach works well. ([PostgreSQL][2])

